# F7 test: G2/G3 arcs carrying extra (ABC) axes.
#
# The extra axes travel linearly alongside the arc and land exactly on the
# commanded values, in every arc plane. The feedrate is the XYZ path rate
# (RS274/NGC): ABC do not contribute to the arc length, they only have to
# start and stop together with the XYZ motion.
#
# See gcode_arcs.test for the upstream (XYZ + E only) coverage, and
# gcode_arcs_abc_unhomed.test for the proof that an arc really moves the
# extra axis it names.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG gcode_arcs_abc.cfg

# Homes XYZ plus the homeable B axis; A and C have no endstop.
G28
G90

# --- XY plane (G17), two extra axes from a non-zero start -----------------
# A starts at 40 and is commanded to 50.  a_stepper tops out at 60, so an
# endpoint computed from the absolute target (40 + 50) instead of the delta
# would land out of range here.
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 A40 C10 F3000
G2 X125 Y32 Z20 A50 C20 I10.5 J10.5

# Same move in the other direction, with B travelling back down.
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 B30 F3000
G3 X125 Y32 Z20 B10 I10.5 J10.5

# Extra axes interpolated across many segments stay within bounds.
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 A60 B50 C100 F3000
G2 X125 Y32 Z20 A0 B-5 C0 I10.5 J10.5

# --- XZ plane (G18) ------------------------------------------------------
G18
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 A10 F3000
G2 X125 Y20 Z32 A20 I10.5 K10.5

# --- YZ plane (G19) ------------------------------------------------------
G19
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 B20 C10 F3000
G2 X20 Y125 Z32 B30 C30 J10.5 K10.5
G17

# --- Helical arc with an extra axis --------------------------------------
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 A10 F3000
G2 X125 Y32 Z30 A20 I10.5 J10.5

# --- Extra axis omitted, or commanded to its current position ------------
# Both leave the axis untouched (a zero-length extra-axis move is dropped).
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 A20 F3000
G2 X125 Y32 Z20 I10.5 J10.5
G2 X20 Y20 Z20 A20 I10.5 J10.5

# --- An arc with extrude plus an extra axis ------------------------------
G1 X20 Y20 Z20 E0 F3000
G2 X125 Y32 Z20 E1 A30 I10.5 J10.5

# --- Letters that are not registered axes are ignored, as in G1 ----------
G2 X20 Y20 Z20 D5 I10.5 J10.5 F3000

# Final positions, including the extra axes.
GET_POSITION
M114

M84
